  "question": {
    "text": "Two stations A and B are 110 km apart on a straight line. One train starts from A at 7 a.m. and travels towards B at 20 kmph. Another train starts from B at 8 a.m. and travels towards A at a speed of 25 kmph. How many hours after the start, the train which starts from station A, will meet the other train which is coming from station B?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Suppose they meet <math><mi>x</mi></math> hours after 7 a.m.<br /><br />Distance covered by A in <math><mi>x</mi></math> hours = 20<math><mi>x</mi></math> km.<br /><br />Distance covered by B in <math><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> hours <math><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>110</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>135</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>hr</mo></math></p>"
  }
}